# rustfmt.toml pins `newline_style = "Unix"`, so the working tree must be LF on every OS.
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true turns every file into CRLF and
# `cargo fmt --check` fails in CI for reasons that have nothing to do with the code.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets keep their bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.der binary
*.crt binary

# A committed `mixengine.db` is a frozen artifact (T89). Git's own heuristic would call it binary —
# a SQLite file opens `SQLite format 3\0` — but "would" is not something to rest a fixture on, and a
# database quietly rewritten by the `text=auto` filter above is a corrupt page and a failure that
# names nothing.
*.db binary
